**Definition 10.2 (The remaining strict joint lift problem).** The
remaining question is whether there exist real $p\ne24,v$ and
four complete worlds with

$$
\begin{gathered}
W_i\in C(p,v)\quad(0\le i\le3),\\
W_0\ne W_1,\quad a(W_0)=a(W_1),\\
W_2\ne W_3,\quad m(W_2)=m(W_3).
\end{gathered}
\tag{10.1}
$$

Cross-pair equality of labels is permitted and the common $a$ and
$m$ need not be equal. Determining the real liftable portions of
the complex curve and their intersections with an independently
chosen strict-real $J$ pair is unresolved. The analytic $M$ arc
used in Theorem 9.1 lies near the SV region
$[56,58]\times[304,305]$, where SV, Theorem 1.1, excludes $D_J$.
It therefore provides the dimension lower bound without resolving
(10.1). An exclusion of (10.1) would have to cover all its original
strata and all real off-$24$ bases.

